things i noticed in the unix version of nh3.0g5+ :
1) upon blindly entering new floors with telepathy you can "see" monsters
    in various locations. when you attempt to identify these monsters by
    cursor you sometimes will get the identification "dark part of a room
    (or ghost)" instead of the proper identification. this appears to happen
    when the monster is in a room that turns out to be unlit.
2) if you kill a Troll and wait 16 moves or so and then eat it you will
    start devouring it and then you'll notice a squirming in your pack. the
    troll has arisen from the dead even though it was partially eaten.
3) sometimes the segments of a long worms tail are invisible even though
    the long worm isn't. you can hit these invisible segments and kill the
    worm. the invisible segments seem to be the ones created before you
    actually encounter the worm and see its head, "w" segment.
4) you can apply a mirror at a Nymph and it will occasionally steal the
    mirror even though it was not adjacent to or near you at the time.
5) eating a large mimic (while invisible) causes you to mimic a treasure chest
    which you, of course, can't see. when you acquire see invisible sometime
    later you notice that you're not human (i.e. "@") but instead a treasure
    chest ("$"). perhaps that could be cured by eating another mimic, i
    haven't tried that yet.
also, there's the business of implicitly picking up something that you start
to eat off the ground. seems like you should be told that you've acquired
the food item or that it should be implicitly dropped if you get interrupted
while eating it. there's similar behavior with regard to looting chests, etc.
beyond your capacity to actually carry the newly acquired objects. the
result is you collapse under load and waste moves undoing things you really
shouldn't have been able to do to begin with.

with regard to the nymph bug (4 above) i suppose it's possible that the nymph
teleports over and single-mindedly steals the mirror but ...

